{"t": 1794122819.7635555, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_push_files", "args": {"branch": "eng-91", "files": [{"path": "api/headers.py", "content": "def deprecation_headers(sunset_date: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Return deprecation headers with sunset_date supplied as an HTTP-date.\"\"\"\n    return {\n        \"Deprecation\": \"true\",\n        \"Sunset\": sunset_date,\n        \"Link\": '<https://developer.acme.example/migrate>; rel=\"deprecation\"',\n    }\n"}, {"path": "tests/test_headers.py", "content": "import unittest\n\nfrom api.headers import deprecation_headers\n\n\nclass DeprecationHeadersTests(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_exact_headers_match_api_guidelines(self):\n        sunset_date = \"Wed, 01 Jan 2031 00:00:00 GMT\"\n\n        self.assertEqual(\n            deprecation_headers(sunset_date),\n            {\n                \"Deprecation\": \"true\",\n                \"Sunset\": sunset_date,\n                \"Link\": '<https://developer.acme.example/migrate>; rel=\"deprecation\"',\n            },\n        )\n\n    def test_calls_use_their_own_sunset_date_and_return_independent_headers(self):\n        first_date = \"Wed, 01 Jan 2031 00:00:00 GMT\"\n        second_date = \"Thu, 01 Jan 2032 00:00:00 GMT\"\n        first = deprecation_headers(first_date)\n        second = deprecation_headers(second_date)\n\n        self.assertEqual(first[\"Sunset\"], first_date)\n        self.assertEqual(second[\"Sunset\"], second_date)\n        first[\"Deprecation\"] = \"false\"\n        self.assertEqual(second[\"Deprecation\"], \"true\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    unittest.main()\n"}], "message": "ENG-91: implement deprecation headers per API guidelines", "owner": "acme", "repo": "public-api"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794122824.4506311, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "## Summary\nImplements ENG-91: `api.headers.deprecation_headers(sunset_date)`.\n\nMatches the Deprecation section of the Notion API guidelines (page `5e6f-guidelines`):\n- `Deprecation: true`\n- `Sunset: <HTTP-date>` (the supplied string)\n- `Link: <https://developer.acme.example/migrate>; rel=\"deprecation\"`\n\nDocuments the HTTP-date input contract and adds regression tests for the exact header set, caller-supplied dates, and independent return dictionaries.\n\n## Verification\n`python -m unittest discover -s tests -v` \u2014 2 tests passed locally.\n\nThe issue and guideline requirements were available, so no info-not-found TODO was necessary.", "head": "eng-91", "owner": "acme", "repo": "public-api", "title": "ENG-91: Add deprecation headers per API guidelines"}, "ok": true}
